Evaluation data
---------------

The software license does not grant rights to third-party datasets or source
annotations. Two historical result archives contained copied annotations and
mixed analysis inputs. They have been removed from the release tree without
assuming redistribution permission. The member-level hash inventory is in
evaluation/release_artifact_inventory.json; see evaluation/RELEASE_DATA.md.
Historical Git revisions still contain those archives and must not be published
as part of a public release. Use a clean export with no inherited Git history.

The evaluation used third-party datasets with independent terms:

  - Corpus A uses 16 repositories under `AmmarWaheed` on the Hugging Face Hub.
    Their exact revisions and source-annotation hashes are recorded in
    evaluation/configs/corpus_a_sources.json. Their Hub card metadata declares
    Apache-2.0; this is a report of the upstream metadata, not a determination
    of rights in all underlying source material.
  - Corpus B is derived from `InternRobotics/RoboInter-Data` at revision
    0208b79c34eca4d214cdb5d07f5ae0f7cc634340. Its card declares CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
    (non-commercial, share-alike) in its community agreement and refers readers
    to the original RoboInter, DROID and RH20T dataset terms. It includes an
    access-form declaration, but the Hub API reported the repository public
    and ungated on 2026-09-08. That observation does not remove the source terms
    or establish permission to redistribute its contents.

See `evaluation/REPRODUCING.md` for details. The clean source export excludes
historical result artifacts and engineering notes as well as Git history.
